<Slide style={{ width: 1280, height: 720, background: '#0A1020', fontFamily: 'Arial', padding: '52px 60px 30px 60px', display: 'flex', flexDirection: 'column' }}>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 12, color: '#4D8DFF', fontWeight: 'bold', letterSpacing: 2.2 }}>10 · CONTRIBUTIONS</Text>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 32, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF', lineHeight: 1.2, marginTop: 8 }}>
        Four workstreams, one shared protocol
    </Text>
    <Box style={{ width: 1160, height: 1, background: '#24334C', marginTop: 14 }} />

    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'column', marginTop: 10 }}>
        {[
            ['Yihui WAN', 'QUESTION · DATA · GPU ARMS',
                'Framed the question and the experiment design; built the frozen splits, the licence ledger and the hash manifests that trace every number to a row; then ran the GPU arms — chemprop 2.1.0 sweep, polyBERT embeddings and the OpenPoly scan.'],
            ['Yixuan ZHOU', 'CLASSICAL ARM FAMILY',
                'Built the classical family: the A1 floor, the descriptor-plus-fingerprint XGBoost with its 30-trial tuning and eight frozen hyperparameters, and the A5 skeleton — one framework with three switches, so two arms differ only by what they are fed.'],
            ['Xingshuai WANG', 'SCALING · TRANSFER SET-UP',
                'Ran the PolyBench26 official n-levels and the OpenPoly classical scan — 265 records in total; then materialised the architecture-transfer splits and the 683 component features, and rebuilt the official floor the transfer stage is measured against.'],
            ['Peng SUN', 'TRANSFER · TABLE · AUDIT',
                'Ran the architecture-transfer arm end to end — 15 runs plus the official three-stage OOD evaluation over 683 components; assembled the 8 × 4 main table, and wrote the audit suite that rejects any run whose provenance fails to reconcile.'],
        ].map(([name, role, body], i) => (
            <Box key={name} style={{ flexDirection: 'row', gap: 32, paddingTop: 32, paddingBottom: 32, borderTop: i === 0 ? '0px solid #1D2A40' : '1px solid #1D2A40' }}>
                <Box style={{ width: 242, flexDirection: 'column' }}>
                    <Text style={{ fontSize: 17, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF', lineHeight: 1.3 }}>{name}</Text>
                    <Text style={{ fontSize: 10, color: '#4D8DFF', marginTop: 5, letterSpacing: 0.8, lineHeight: 1.5 }}>{role}</Text>
                </Box>
                <Text style={{ flex: 1, fontSize: 13.5, color: '#A8B8CE', lineHeight: 1.7 }}>{body}</Text>
            </Box>
        ))}
    </Box>

    <Box style={{ marginTop: 'auto', flexDirection: 'row', gap: 40 }}>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 12, color: '#7E93AE', flex: 1, lineHeight: 1.6 }}>
            Shared rule across all four: same features, same splits, seeds 0 / 1 / 2. Nobody may change these three, which is why the arms are comparable at all.
        </Text>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 12, color: '#7E93AE', lineHeight: 1.6 }}>
            962 run records in one ledger, each with its predictions and hashes.
        </Text>
    </Box>

    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', justifyContent: 'space-between', marginTop: 10 }}>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 12, color: '#5E7590' }}>Group 32 · How Much Is a Chain Worth?</Text>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 12, color: '#5E7590' }}>16 / 17</Text>
    </Box>
</Slide>
